==English==

===Etymology===
{{unk.|en}}. Various unlikely theories derive it from "fucked up, got ambushed, zipped in [a body bag]" (if this is not simply a [[backronym]]), {{etyl|fr|-}} {{term|fougasse||land mine|lang=fr}} or English ''[[fugacious]]''. Derivation from an Italian word *{{term||fugazi|fake|lang=it}} is sometimes suggested, but no such word exists in Italian.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/fuɡɑzi/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|?}}

